We have
$$
\begin{aligned}
\prod_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{(2*k)^2}{(2*k-1)(2*k+1)} &=\prod_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{4*k^2}{(2*k-1)(2*k+1)} \\
&=\prod_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{4}{2*k+1}\frac{k}{2*k-1} \\
&=\prod_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{2}{2*k-1}\frac{k}{2*k-1} \\
&=\prod_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{2}{2*k-1} \\
&= \frac{2}{1}\frac{2}{3}\frac{3}{5}\frac{4}{7} \frac{5}{7} \frac{6}{9} \frac{7}{9} \frac{8}{11} \dotsb \\
&=\frac{2}{1}\frac{2}{3}\frac{4}{5} \frac{6}{7} \frac{8}{9} \dotsb \\
&= 2\left(\frac{1}{1}\frac{2}{2}\frac{3}{3}\frac{4}{4} \dotsb\right) \\
&=2 \left(1\right) \\
&=2
\end{aligned}
$$
Therefore,
$$
\frac{2}{\pi} \prod_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{(2*k)^2}{(2*k-1)(2*k+1)} = \frac{2}{\pi} \cdot 2= \frac{4}{\pi} \approx 1.27324
$$
